title: The Palace Protest
new-page: true

= October 1949

Reports of manipulation in the elections to the Sixteenth Majles have brought
Mohammad Mossadegh and other opposition politicians together. They prepare a
protest at the royal palace. The loose cooperation formed around this electoral
struggle will become the National Front.

This opening establishes the coalition's first shared purpose: representative
elections.

*Research note: Mari Nukii, “Protest Events in the Tehran Bazaar during the Oil
Nationalization Movement of Iran,”* Annals of Japan Association for Middle East
Studies *28, no. 1 (2012), p. 10. Nukii dates the protest to 14 October and
describes Mossadegh and nineteen other politicians organizing against royal and
royalist manipulation of the Sixteenth Majles election. Other chronologies vary
by a day, so the game does not assign a day at this stage.*

